**🟡 Bug: No initialization of fields from existing data on edit**

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js` **Line:** 18

The `initializeExistingFields` method only checks if fields exist in the DOM but doesn't populate them from the model's `specification_pdp` JSON. When editing a product, the dynamic fields won't show existing specification data.

**Current Code:**
```javascript
initializeExistingFields() {
  // Check if there are existing fields in the container
  const existingFields = this.containerTarget.querySelectorAll('[data-field-index]')
  this.fieldCount = existingFields.length

  // If no existing fields, add one empty field
  if (this.fieldCount === 0) {
    this.addField()
  }
}
```

**Suggested Fix:**
```javascript
initializeExistingFields() {
  // Load existing data from hidden field
  const hiddenField = document.querySelector('[name="product[specification_pdp]"]')
  if (hiddenField && hiddenField.value) {
    try {
      const specs = JSON.parse(hiddenField.value)
      Object.entries(specs).forEach(([group, items]) => {
        items.forEach(item => {
          this.addFieldWithData(group, item.name, item.value)
        })
      })
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Failed to parse existing specifications:', e)
    }
  }

  if (this.fieldCount === 0) {
    this.addField()
  }
}
```

**Recommendation:** Implement proper initialization logic to populate fields from existing JSON data when editing a product. Add a new method `addFieldWithData(group, name, value)` that creates a field row with pre-filled values.

---
